{
  "rules_version": "1.1.0",
  "effective_from": "2026-10-29",
  "_comment": [
    "Analysis categories for the price-position comparison (ADR-006).",
    "Price-INDEPENDENT by construction: the only inputs are the product title, the URL path and the",
    "shop's own section slugs. Price, old price, sale state and currency are never read.",
    "Deliberately NOT used as signals, because they describe price or an occasion rather than a product",
    "type: nedorogie-czvety / nedorogie (price band), aktsii-* / topsale / sale (promotions),",
    "8-marta / 14-fevralya / novyj-god (occasions). A listing that carries only such slugs falls through",
    "to the title rules, and is counted as unclassified if the title says nothing either.",
    "Matching: titles and URL paths are lower-cased, punctuation becomes spaces, and a keyword matches",
    "only as a whole word or whole phrase. Section slugs must match exactly.",
    "First matching rule wins; exclusions are tried before sections.",
    "This file is versioned and tagged before any analysis run; changes get a new rules_version.",
    "1.1.0: S05 also matches the words 'букет' / 'композиция' in a title. Secret's channel captions are marketing lines with no section slug ('Прекрасные букеты для любимой'), so without this rule most of its offers were unclassified. These are product-type words, not price, promotion or occasion words, so the price-independence of the rules is unchanged.",
    "1.1.0: the lexicon also lists instrumental/plural forms ('с тюльпанами и пионами'), which the channel captions use constantly; whole-word matching means each form must be listed explicitly.",
    "1.1.0: section lists also hold the plain Russian section names ('Букеты', 'Растения'), because kamilas.uz publishes its category as schema.org text rather than as a URL slug."
  ],
  "fields_used": [
    "title",
    "url_path",
    "site_category"
  ],
  "categories": {
    "roses_mono": "Roses and mono-bouquets (one named flower type)",
    "mixed_bouquets": "Mixed bouquets (two or more named flower types)",
    "bouquets_unspecified": "Bouquets whose composition is not stated in the listing or post",
    "boxes_baskets": "Flowers in boxes and baskets",
    "potted_plants": "Potted / houseplants",
    "edible_sets": "Edible and berry sets (strawberries in chocolate, sweets, fruit)",
    "out_of_scope": "Explicitly excluded: not a flower, plant or edible product",
    "unclassified": "No rule matched; excluded from analysis and reported as a count"
  },
